1.2 ELP 2000-82B lunar theory series -- M. Chapront-Touze & J. Chapront
    Used in: crates/fe-core/src/points/elp_main.rs (generated by
    tools/gen_intp_series.py; 918 terms, natural apogee/perigee).
    References: A&A 124, 50 (1983); A&A 190, 342 (1988); notice "Lunar
    solution ELP 2000-82B", G. Francou, Bureau des Longitudes (1996).
    Original data: IMCCE - Observatoire de Paris,
    ftp://ftp.imcce.fr/pub/ephem/moon/elp82b/ (files ELP1-ELP36; also CDS
    VI/79); checksums in docs/FICTITIOUS_BODIES.md. No licence statement in
    the distribution [UNCONFIRMED for commercial redistribution].
    The default mean node and mean perigee polynomials (points.rs) are the
    published ELP/MPP02 mean elements: J. Chapront, M. Chapront-Touze &
    G. Francou (2002), A&A 387, 700; J. Chapront & G. Francou (2003),
    A&A 404, 735 (coefficients transcribed from the papers).

1.3 Vondrak, Capitaine & Wallace (2011) long-term precession
    Used in: crates/fe-core/src/ayanamsa/vondrak.rs, frames.rs (series
    PQPOL/PQPER/XYPOL/XYPER and the long-term epsilon_A series).
    Reference: J. Vondrak, N. Capitaine & P. Wallace (2011), "New precession
    expressions, valid for long time intervals", A&A 534, A22; erratum
    A&A 541, C1 (2012). Published coefficients, transcribed from the paper.

1.4 Kinoshita (1975) precession formulation
    Used in: crates/fe-core/src/ayanamsa/orig_precession.rs (SIDBIT_PREC_ORIG
    only). Reference: H. Kinoshita (1975), "Formulas for precession",
    Smithsonian Astrophysical Observatory Special Report 364. Published
    coefficients, transcribed from the report.


