3. STAR CATALOGUE (crates/fe-core/src/stars/catalog.rs, ayanamsa/star.rs)
==============================================================================

3.1 IAU Catalog of Star Names (IAU Working Group on Star Names, WGSN)
    -- Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
    Machine-readable edition by E. Mamajek,
    https://www.pas.rochester.edu/~emamajek/WGSN/IAU-CSN.txt (2022-04-04).
    Attribution: "Star names: IAU Catalog of Star Names, IAU Working Group on
    Star Names (WGSN), https://www.iau.org/public/themes/naming_stars/,
    licensed under CC BY 4.0." Changes: names are matched case- and
    space-insensitively and combined with traditional aliases and classic
    "Name,nomenclature" display strings.

3.2 Hipparcos, the New Reduction (ESA) [UNCONFIRMED for commercial redistribution]
    Positions, proper motions and parallaxes at J1991.25 for the HIP stars.
    Reference: F. van Leeuwen (2007), "Validation of the new Hipparcos
    reduction", A&A 474, 653 (CDS catalogue I/311, retrieved from the CDS
    VizieR service). Some V magnitudes from The Hipparcos and Tycho Catalogues
    (ESA 1997, ESA SP-1200; CDS catalogue I/239), field H5.
    Acknowledgement: "This product uses data from the ESA Hipparcos mission."
    ESA scientific data are free to use with acknowledgement; explicit
    confirmation of commercial-redistribution terms is pending.

3.3 SIMBAD astronomical database (CDS, Strasbourg) [UNCONFIRMED for commercial redistribution]
    Radial velocities, V magnitudes, and the places/motions of the objects
    without a Hipparcos 2007 solution; each value's bibcode is stored in the
    record's rv_ref field and credits the original publication (among them
    Gontcharov 2006, CDS III/252; Kharchenko et al. 2007; Famaey et al. 2005;
    Nordstrom et al. 2004; Ducati 2002, CDS II/237). Open-cluster places and
    motions: Dias et al. (2002), A&A 389, 871 (CDS catalogue B/ocl, version 3.5).
    Acknowledgement requested by CDS: "This research has made use of the
    SIMBAD database, operated at CDS, Strasbourg, France."
    Reference: M. Wenger et al. (2000), A&AS 143, 9.

3.4 Gaia (ESA) -- not used
    The catalogue contains no value from the Gaia mission (DR1, DR2, EDR3, DR3)
    or from publications derived from Gaia data, so the CC BY-SA 3.0 IGO terms
    of Gaia data do not apply. tools/build_stars.py rejects Gaia-derived
    sources (Gaia releases and a list of Gaia-based publications) and the test
    tests/stars.rs::no_gaia_derived_values_in_catalogue enforces it; the values
    that were replaced are listed in tools/star_gaia_replacements.tsv.

3.5 Other published values in the catalogue: alpha Cen masses (Kervella et
    al. 2016, A&A 594, A107), parallax (Akeson et al. 2021, AJ 162, 14); Sgr A*
    proper motion (Reid & Brunthaler 2004, ApJ 616, 872; 2020, ApJ 892, 39);
    R0 (GRAVITY Collaboration 2019, A&A 625, L10); galactic poles (Liu, Zhu &
    Zhang 2011, A&A 526, A16); invariable plane (Souami & Souchay 2012, A&A
    543, A133); delta Cnc RV (Massarotti et al. 2008, AJ 135, 209).

3.6 Star names in the default catalogue
    Names come only from the IAU WGSN list (3.1), SIMBAD "NAME" identifiers
    (3.3) and traditional names from R. H. Allen, "Star-Names and Their
    Meanings" (1899, public domain); designations are in standard form.
    An optional compatibility alias table with the classic names and
    "Name,nomenclature" strings of earlier astrology software is NOT part of
    this distribution: it is built privately (tools/build_star_compat.py) and
    loaded at runtime only if a deployment supplies it
    (FRENCHEPHEMERIS_STAR_COMPAT).


