5. PUBLISHED THEORIES AND DEFINITIONS (references, not licences)
==============================================================================

The following works define methods or constants that FrenchEphemeris
implements from the publication. They are cited for scholarship; no text or
code is copied from them. Full per-constant provenance is in
docs/GEOMETRY_REPORT.md (Provenance), docs/EVENTS_REPORT.md section 5,
docs/HELIACAL_REPORT.md section 1, docs/FICTITIOUS_BODIES.md and
docs/TIME_FRAMES_REPORT.md.

- Astronomy: IAU 2000/2006 resolutions; IERS Conventions (2003, 2010);
  Capitaine, Wallace & Chapront (2003); Lieske et al. (1977) and Lieske
  (1979); Wahr (1981); Seidelmann (1982); Simon et al. (1994); Fairhead &
  Bretagnon (1990); Explanatory Supplement to the Astronomical Almanac
  (1961, 1992); Meeus, Astronomical Algorithms (2nd ed.); Mallama & Hilton
  (2018); IAU WGCCRE 2015 (Archinal et al. 2018); Sinclair (1982), NAO TN 59;
  Bennett (1982); Saemundsson (1986); Schaefer (1990, 1993, 1998, program
  VISLIMIT); Yallop (1997), NAO TN 69; Danjon's shadow rule.
- House systems: Placidus, Koch, Porphyry, Regiomontanus, Campanus,
  Topocentric (Polich & Page), equal and whole-sign systems, Alcabitius,
  Meridian, Carter poli-equatorial (Carter 1947), Morinus, Horizon,
  Krusinski-Pisa-Goelzer, APC, Pullen SD/SR, Sripati, Sunshine (Makransky),
  Savard-A (J. Savard), Gauquelin sectors (M. Gauquelin).
- Ayanamsas: Lahiri (Indian Calendar Reform Committee 1955; Indian
  Astronomical Ephemeris 1985), Fagan-Bradley, Raman, Krishnamurti,
  Yukteshwar, True Pushya (P. V. R. Narasimha Rao), galactic-centre and
  galactic-equator variants, and the other sidereal modes with the authors
  cited in docs/GEOMETRY_REPORT.md section 2.
- Hypothetical bodies: J. Neely (1980), Matrix Journal VII (Uranian planets);
  R. S. Harrington (1988), AJ 96, 1476; Le Verrier (1846); J. C. Adams
  (1846); P. Lowell (1915) via E. C. Bower (1931); P. Globa (Selena);
  "Dr. Waltemath's Moon", Monthly Weather Review 26 (1898).
- Classic astrology-engine API semantics: the Swiss Ephemeris programmer's
  documentation is cited in several modules as the
  description of the classic API's behaviour and of the published methods it
  uses. The documentation is copyrighted by its owner; it is referenced,
  not reproduced.


